  "feature_importance": {
    "file": "data/processed/ml_feature_importance.tsv",
    "method": "L2 logistic regression refitted on all samples of each analysis (binary task), top-k variance genes computed on all samples, standardised; coefficients > 0 point toward simulated microgravity. Top 25 genes by |coefficient| per analysis and k, with the number of LOOCV training folds in which each gene was selected and kept the same coefficient sign.",
    "status": "descriptive only, not validated. With n = 8 or 9 and k >> n the coefficients are heavily shrunk and spread over correlated genes, so the ranking is unstable and is not a biomarker list. No importances are reported for TabPFN or the random forest."
  },
  "osd90_cross_study_transfer": "not performed",
  "caveats": [
    "n is 8 (primary) or 9 (sensitivity) samples; each LOOCV fold trains on 7 or 8 samples. Accuracy moves in steps of 1/8 or 1/9.",
    "The permutation p-value cannot go below min_attainable_p, so even a perfect LOOCV score is weak evidence on its own.",
    "LOOCV with tiny classes penalises classifiers that lean on class frequencies: holding out a sample shrinks its class in the training fold. The majority baseline shows the resulting no-information level (it can sit below chance), and the permutation null includes this effect.",
    "AUROC is computed from held-out probabilities pooled across LOOCV folds, which come from different fitted models; treat it as descriptive.",
    "The three-class task has 2 (primary) or 3 (sensitivity) RPM samples.",
    "The VST was fitted by DESeq2 with blind = TRUE on all samples of each analysis, the held-out one included. It does not use labels, so it cannot leak class information, but it is not refitted per fold.",
    "Top-k genes are chosen by unsupervised variance, not by association with the labels; k = 50 and k = 200 are both reported and neither was tuned.",
    "The sensitivity analysis adds RFPRPM4, a library inferred from the deposited RFPRPM4 files (which begin with the complete RFPRPM41 files); it may not be an independent biological replicate.",
    "TabPFN v2 is used because the package default (TabPFN-3) requires a Prior Labs account and licence acceptance; later TabPFN versions may give different results.",
    "OSD-90 cross-study transfer was not performed; this analysis supports no claim about transfer to other studies."
  ],
